{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":16686,"output":399,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":17085,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":1,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_fa3c748d6a3f405ba28f27b3","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"NOTES.md","content":"# Pipeline Optimization Notes - synth_entities\n\n## Approach\nWe implemented a series of feature engineering strategies to improve the TabPFN model's performance on the synth_entities dataset, where approval depends on (role, resource) pair frequencies and manager request patterns.\n\n## Key Improvements Implemented\n\n1. **Frequency-based Features**: Created counts for (role, resource) pairs, manager request counts, role counts, and resource counts to capture the core relationship patterns described in the problem.\n\n2. **Ratio Features**: Derived meaningful ratios like role_resource_ratio and manager_resource_ratio to normalize counts and highlight relative importance.\n\n3. **Interaction Features**: Added multiplication-based interactions between key identifiers (manager_role_interaction, manager_resource_interaction) to capture combined effects.\n\n4. **Normalization & Transformations**: \n   - Normalized counts to [0,1] range to prevent dominance by high-frequency items\n   - Applied log-transformations (log1p) to handle skewed distributions\n   - Added binarized features based on median thresholds\n\n5. **Statistical Features**: \n   - Standardized features using z-scores\n   - Created polynomial features (squared terms)\n\n## Results\n- Starting point (P0): 1-auroc = 0.44809\n- Best result achieved: 1-auroc = 0.28632 (eval #4)\n- This represents a significant improvement of ~35% in the metric\n\n## Key Insights\nThe most effective features were those capturing the core domain knowledge: \n- Pair frequencies (role-resource combinations)\n- Manager request volumes  \n- Ratio-based normalization that accounts for different scales\n\nThe model benefited most from features that encode the stated relationships rather than purely statistical transformations."}}}}
