{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":17269,"output":347,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":17616,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"I've successfully optimized the pipeline for the synth_entities dataset. Here's a summary of what was accomplished:\n\n## What I Did\n\n1. **Analyzed the Dataset**: Examined the synthetic access-request approval data with 4 categorical columns (role_id, manager_id, resource_id, request_id) and binary target (approved).\n\n2. **Implemented Feature Engineering**: Created multiple types of features that capture the domain knowledge:\n   - Frequency counts for role-resource pairs and manager requests\n   - Ratio features that normalize these counts\n   - Interaction features combining identifiers\n   - Log-transformed features to handle skewness\n   - Binarized features based on medians\n\n3. **Optimized Through Iteration**: Tested several variations and settled on the best performing version that achieved:\n   - 1-auroc = 0.28632 (best result)\n   - Started from baseline of 1-auroc = 0.44809\n   - Improvement of ~35% in the evaluation metric\n\n## Key Features Created\n\n- role_resource_count: Frequency of (role, resource) pairs\n- manager_request_count: Number of requests per manager\n- role_resource_ratio: Normalized pair frequency\n- manager_resource_ratio: Normalized manager request frequency\n- log_role_resource_count: Log-transformed pair frequency\n- high_role_resource: Binary indicator for high-frequency pairs\n- Various interaction and statistical features\n\nThe final pipeline is in `pipeline.py` and documentation of the approach is in `NOTES.md`. The solution respects all constraints - it only modifies the pipeline.py file, uses only the allowed libraries, and doesn't hard-code label information or replace the frozen model."}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've successfully optimized the pipeline for the synth_entities dataset. Here's a summary of what was accomplished:\n\n## What I Did\n\n1. **Analyzed the Dataset**: Examined the synthetic access-request approval data with 4 categorical columns (role_id, manager_id, resource_id, request_id) and binary target (approved).\n\n2. **Implemented Feature Engineering**: Created multiple types of features that capture the domain knowledge:\n   - Frequency counts for role-resource pairs and manager requests\n   - Ratio features that normalize these counts\n   - Interaction features combining identifiers\n   - Log-transformed features to handle skewness\n   - Binarized features based on medians\n\n3. **Optimized Through Iteration**: Tested several variations and settled on the best performing version that achieved:\n   - 1-auroc = 0.28632 (best result)\n   - Started from baseline of 1-auroc = 0.44809\n   - Improvement of ~35% in the evaluation metric\n\n## Key Features Created\n\n- role_resource_count: Frequency of (role, resource) pairs\n- manager_request_count: Number of requests per manager\n- role_resource_ratio: Normalized pair frequency\n- manager_resource_ratio: Normalized manager request frequency\n- log_role_resource_count: Log-transformed pair frequency\n- high_role_resource: Binary indicator for high-frequency pairs\n- Various interaction and statistical features\n\nThe final pipeline is in `pipeline.py` and documentation of the approach is in `NOTES.md`. The solution respects all constraints - it only modifies the pipeline.py file, uses only the allowed libraries, and doesn't hard-code label information or replace the frozen model."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vllm","model":"Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct","usage":{"input":17269,"output":347,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":17616,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"tota